          bobResponse: 'Compliance escalation case built.\n\n**Regulatory exposure:**\n• PCI DSS Requirement 10.2: "Implement audit trails to reconstruct... activities." Silent log failures mean undetected gaps — a direct PCI DSS 10.2 violation.\n• PSD2 (if EU): Article 96 requires audit trails for all payment transactions. Missing logs = reportable incident.\n• Internal SLA: your audit policy (section 4.3) requires 100% log coverage for all financial transactions.\n\n**Risk if shipped as-is:** A single failed audit write creates an undetected gap. In the event of a dispute or fraud investigation, you cannot reconstruct the transaction — exposing the company to regulatory fines and legal liability.\n\n**Recommended escalation path:** Re-classify bug severity to Critical/Blocker. Escalate to Engineering Lead and Compliance Officer. Do not ship until resolved.',
